@startuml use_case_diagram
title ArtistConnect - Use Case Diagram (Iteration 1)

' ---- Use case diagram conventions ----
' - The rectangle is the system boundary: everything the system is
'   responsible for goes inside it. Actors stay outside.
' - <<include>> = the base use case ALWAYS triggers the included one.
' - <<extend>>  = the extending use case is OPTIONAL / conditional.
' - Update this diagram whenever a teammate's use cases below change.

left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor Fan
actor Artist
actor Admin

rectangle "ArtistConnect System" {

  ' --- Alejandro Garcia Jr's use cases ---
  usecase "Search for Artist" as UC_Search
  usecase "Start Direct Chat" as UC_Chat
  usecase "Follow Artist" as UC_Follow
  usecase "Request Booking" as UC_Book
  usecase "Review Report" as UC_Report
  usecase "Create Event" as UC_CreateEvent
  usecase "Review Event Pricing" as UC_ReviewPricing

  ' --- Placeholder use cases for remaining team members ---
  usecase "[Teammate 2 - UC 1]" as UC_T2_1 #line.dashed
  usecase "[Teammate 2 - UC 2]" as UC_T2_2 #line.dashed
  usecase "[Teammate 2 - UC 3]" as UC_T2_3 #line.dashed
  usecase "[Teammate 3 - UC 1]" as UC_T3_1 #line.dashed
  usecase "[Teammate 3 - UC 2]" as UC_T3_2 #line.dashed
  usecase "[Teammate 3 - UC 3]" as UC_T3_3 #line.dashed
}

Fan --> UC_Search
Fan --> UC_Chat
Fan --> UC_Follow
Fan --> UC_Book
Fan --> UC_Report

Artist --> UC_CreateEvent
Artist --> UC_Report
Artist --> UC_Chat

Admin --> UC_Report
Admin --> UC_ReviewPricing

UC_Search .> UC_Chat : <<extend>>
UC_Search .> UC_Follow : <<extend>>
UC_Search .> UC_Book : <<extend>>
UC_CreateEvent .> UC_ReviewPricing : <<include>>

Fan -[hidden]- UC_T2_1
Artist -[hidden]- UC_T3_1

@enduml
